WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.128
The most striking finding comes from analysing the
kernel-regression solution.

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:07.064
With Jacobian regularisation,

00:00:07.144 --> 00:00:11.203
the eigenfeatures that are more accurate are also
more robust;

00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:13.740
accuracy and robustness move together.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.678
Standard training shows almost no such link,

00:00:16.758 --> 00:00:22.553
and it never produces the accurate-but-fragile
features seen in earlier finite-NTK work.

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:27.293
So the regulariser isn't just trading a little
accuracy for robustness;

00:00:27.373 --> 00:00:28.495
it aligns the two.

00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:34.437
A separate check on the key full-rank assumption
shows it is fragile: the JNTK's smallest

00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:39.778
eigenvalue is far below the NTK's and only becomes
positive for deeper networks,

00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:43.650
depth eleven for GeLU but just six for the erf activation.
